{"requisitesSimple": [{"id": "admreq", "name": "Admission Requirements", "requirementLevel": "programAdmissionRequirements", "rules": [], "showInCatalog": true, "sisId": "", "type": "Completion Requirements"}, {"id": "082331511", "name": "Program Requirements", "requirementLevel": "programRequirements", "rules": [{"condition": "completedAnyOf", "credits": 14, "description": "<p>Plan A students must complete a minimum of 20 credits. Plan B students must complete a minimum of 27 credits. For both Plan A and Plan B students, at least 14 credits must be from RSC courses (see list below). RSC 5106 Introduction to Rehabilitation Science is required for both Plan A and Plan B students. Remaining required credits are electives. All courses taken must be graduate level (5xxx level or greater; 4xxx level courses are not allowed). All courses should be taken in consultation with the student's advisor.<br></p>", "id": "418515", "minCredits": 14, "name": "Coursework ", "value": {"condition": "courses", "id": "418515", "subSelections": [], "values": [{"logic": "and", "value": ["8112061"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8180261"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8180251"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8087691"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0107851"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8074971"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8045761"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8105751"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0107931"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8252801"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8140521"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8152101"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8188191"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8254251"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0102721"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8204831"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8140531"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0094821"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0107921"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0107991"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0108001"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0111571"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0108121"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8113751"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8055941"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["7899111"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8129561"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8251271"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["8252781"]}]}}, {"condition": "minimumCredits", "credits": 3, "description": "All master's students must take one of the two statistics courses below, or another statistics course approved by the advisor, for at least three credits.", "id": "418516", "name": "Statistics Requirement (3 credits)", "value": {"condition": "courses", "id": "418516", "subSelections": [], "values": [{"logic": "and", "value": ["8069381"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0028061"]}]}}, {"condition": "minimumCredits", "credits": 10, "description": "Take at least 10 master's thesis credits.", "id": "418517", "name": "Plan A", "value": {"condition": "courses", "id": "418517", "subSelections": [], "values": [{"logic": "and", "value": ["7886541"]}]}}, {"condition": "allOf", "id": "418518", "name": "Plan B", "notes": "<p>Regarding the Plan B Project, students pursuing the MS Plan B degree must demonstrate familiarity with the tools of research or scholarship in their major field, the ability to work independently, and the ability to present the results of their investigation effectively, by completing at least one Plan B project. The Plan B project(s) should involve a combined total of approximately 120 hours of work. The student’s advisor specifies both the nature and extent of the options available to satisfy this requirement, and whether the requirement is to be satisfied in conjunction with, or independent of, the courses in the student’s program.</p>", "subRules": [{"condition": "completedAnyOf", "id": "bYL0XFRB", "name": "Plan B Project", "value": {"condition": "courses", "id": "pJE2U4FM", "subSelections": [], "values": [{"logic": "and", "value": ["0107931"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0107991"]}, {"logic": "and", "value": ["0108001"]}]}}]}, {"condition": "minimumCredits", "credits": 1, "description": "<p>Completion of RSC 5106 counts toward the 14 required RSC credits for Plan B students.</p>", "id": "cxcMOvMd", "name": "Required Course RSC 5106 (1 credit)", "value": {"condition": "courses", "id": "KalcEoVG", "subSelections": [], "values": [{"logic": "and", "value": ["8140511"]}]}}], "showInCatalog": true, "sisId": "", "type": "Completion Requirements"}, {"id": "87775", "name": "Integrated BS-Biomedical Engineering/MS-Rehabilitation Science", "notes": "<p>The Integrated BS Biomedical Engineering / MS Rehabilitation Science program offers students the opportunity to earn a bachelor's degree and a master's degree in a shortened amount of time. The integrated program offers several benefits, including streamlined admissions from the undergraduate to the graduate program, and flexibility in fulfilling required courses for both degrees during the senior year.

<br>Students pursuing the integrated BS/MS may complete either the Plan A or Plan B option for the Rehabilitation Science master's degree. Both the BS and MS degrees must be completed in their entirety, with no courses shared between them. The graduate degree cannot be earned before the undergraduate requirements are satisfied. Admitted students who decide not to complete the MS degree may count credits originally planned for the graduate program toward their BS degree with approval of the Biomedical Engineering advisors.

<br>For more information regarding the integrated BS/MS degree, including eligibility requirements, contact the Biomedical Engineering or Rehabilitation Science program office.<br></p>", "requirementLevel": "programSubPlanRequirements", "rules": [], "showInCatalog": true, "sisId": "", "type": "Completion Requirements"}]}

