s for a career in research, teaching, or industry within the field of stem cell biology. It offers training in stem cell biology, a rapidly growing interdisciplinary field that rests on foundations provided by molecular, cellular, and developmental biology. Students will take lecture, lab, and seminar courses in these various disciplines, in addition to stem cell biology. They will interact with members of the Stem Cell Institute through participation in research seminars and journal clubs.  

Students who elect Plan A will spend a full calendar year, including summer, conducting  research in the laboratory of a stem cell graduate program faculty member. This research will form the basis of the master's thesis. 

Students who elect Plan B will conduct research of primary literature resulting in a written paper and seminar on a topic in Stem Cell Biology agreed upon in advance by the student and faculty advisor. Part-time students choosing Plan B are expected to complete the degree within 3 years by taking take one to two courses per semester, excluding summers.", "cdProgramDisplayCatalog": true, "cdProgramDualDeg": false, "cdProgramFieldofStudy": "Math, Engineering, and Science", "cdProgramGPAGoodStanding": "2.800", "cdProgramGradMinor4xxx": true, "cdProgramGradResGradProf": "Graduate Research", "cdProgramLOs": "The goals of this program are to address five aspects of student learning: 1) a solid knowledge base, 2) critical thinking skills, 3) technical laboratory skills (for Plan A students), 4) communication skills, and 5) professional responsibility.", "cdProgramLengthInTermsGrad": "3", "cdProgramMastPlanA": true, "cdProgramMastPlanACrMax": 30, "cdProgramMastPlanACrMin": "20", "cdProgramMastPlanACrThesis": "10", "cdProgramMastPlanAFinExDesc": "Oral Examination Only", "cdProgramMastPlanB": true, "cdProgramMastPlanBCap": false, "cdProgramMastPlanBCrMax": "30", "cdProgramMastPlanBCrMin": "30", "cdProgramMastPlanBFinEx": "Oral examination only", "cdProgramMastPlanC": false, "cdProgramMinorAllowed": true, "cdProgramNameShort": "StemCellBi", "cdProgramReqLanguageGrad": false, "cdProgramReqSubplanGrad": false, "cdProgramStatus": "Active", "cdProgramSubplanMoreThanOne": false, "cdProgramSumTerms": false, "cdProgramTypeManual": "Master's", "cdProgramWebsite": "https://med.umn.edu/stemcell/graduate-programs/master-science-stem-cell-biology", "g9JMc": false, "o8EfQ": false, "programLevelCareer": "Graduate", "reportAsNscProgram": true, "sJszy": false, "saaWhifDispAdvr": true, "saaWhifDispPrem": true, "saaWhifDispStd": true, "splitOwnership": false, "status": "Active"}

