A final capstone project integrates students’ learning throughout the program and provides an opportunity to design an in-depth project tailored to students’ interests and professional goals while serving the needs of a particular organization or group in the community and/or addressing an important social issue. 

Please note: We are not currently accepting applications as we work through program and curriculum updates.", "cdProgramDisplayCatalog": true, "cdProgramDualDeg": false, "cdProgramGPAGoodStanding": "2.8", "cdProgramGradMinor4xxx": true, "cdProgramGradResGradProf": "Graduate Professional", "cdProgramLOs": "<p>Graduates of the CIVE program achieve the following learning goals by the end of their program</p><ol type="1"><li><p>Develop self-awareness and appreciation of multifaceted perspectives to exercise ethical activism, leadership and/or allyship to achieve shared goals.</p></li><li><p>Evaluate theories and historical traditions of community organizing, change processes, interventions, movements, and strategies to inform creative thinking and strategic actions that address the challenges of today and tomorrow.</p></li><li><p>Understand the political, economic, power, and spatial environments within which community and civic actions take place to inform development of appropriate goals and strategies.</p></li><li><p>Analyze structures and processes of communities and institutions including public, private, nonprofit, and voluntary interests to impact decision-making and capacity building.</p></li><li><p>Develop strategies and tactics to inform and build power and capacity within communities to effectively participate in critical decision-making and actions, and to apply appropriate leadership approaches within change movements.</p></li><li><p>Create formal methods to understand, evaluate, and shape social change strategies and to assess strengths and limitations of civic engagement and action strategies in community and organizational contexts.</p></li></ol>", "cdProgramLengthInTermsGrad": "6", "cdProgramMastPlanA": false, "cdProgramMastPlanB": false, "cdProgramMastPlanC": true, "cdProgramMastPlanCCap": true, "cdProgramMastPlanCCapDesc": "The capstone course (CIVE 6002) synthesizes the completed disciplinary and applied business coursework, and facilitates completion of an individualized, applied project based on the student's community-engagement career focus. This culminating experience, taken in the final year of the program, provides students with an opportunity to engage in creative problem solving to address pressing real-world needs.", "cdProgramMastPlanCCrMax": "30", "cdProgramMastPlanCCrMin": "30", "cdProgramMastPlanCHasFinEx": false, "cdProgramMinorAllowed": true, "cdProgramNameShort": "Civic Eng", "cdProgramReqLanguageGrad": false, "cdProgramReqSubplanGrad": true, "cdProgramStatus": "Active", "cdProgramSubplanMoreThanOne": false, "cdProgramSumTerms": false, "cdProgramTypeManual": "Master's", "cdProgramWebsite": "<p><a href="https://ccaps.umn.edu/civic-engagement-masters-degree" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">https://ccaps.umn.edu/civic-engagement-masters-degree</a></p>", "feV9J": "<p>Internal faculty/program discussions and desire to conform to University standard. </p>", "g9JMc": false, "o8EfQ": false, "programLevelCareer": "Graduate", "reportAsNscProgram": true, "sJszy": false, "saaWhifDispAdvr": false, "saaWhifDispPrem": false, "saaWhifDispStd": false, "splitOwnership": false, "status": "Active"}

